<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Equations of Two Lines and a Curve</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02534</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Equations of Two Lines and a Curve</md:title>
    <md:uuid>dc0475e3-949f-42ba-b53a-eb33dd135017</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Write an equation representing the line that passes through each pair of points.
          <list class="os-raise-noindent" number-style="lower-alpha" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00002">
            <item><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></item>
            <item><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>Solve this equation: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. Show your reasoning.</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>